{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1545870-factions-tier-2-curseborne-play","id":1545870,"title":"Factions, Tier 2 Curseborne Play","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-14T12:54:34-08:00","id":1545870,"title":"Factions, Tier 2 Curseborne Play","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I\u2019ve mentioned in other threads that I think Secret Societies and organizations, factions really, are something that could bring a lot more depth to the world of Curseborne. In a lot of ways I see them as being a sort of \u201cTier 2\u201d level of play, for when you\u2019re graduating past the street level parts of the game.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I wanted to show my own idea of how this could work with a sample faction. The faction gives the idea of what they\u2019re about, how they recruit, how they\u2019re organized and ends even with some sample rituals.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I might decide to create some more here if there\u2019s any interest, and of course, I\u2019d love to hear comments and see your own ideas on factions and groups that could expand the world of Curseborne!</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>The Sisterhood</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u201c<i>Groups like the Sisterhood have been around forever. As long as there\u2019s been women there\u2019s been men trying to control them, and just as long there\u2019s been women trying to help one another out. We\u2019ve existed in different forms across generations and cultures. Sometimes we\u2019ve been ascendant, influencing entire tribes, nations and empires behind the scenes. Sometimes we\u2019ve been entirely wiped out, left as nothing but ashes for future women to find, and rekindle. There will always be a need for women to look out for one another.</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Look, it\u2019s like this, right? Here in the West, on paper, women are afforded all the rights men are in most nations\u2026 but the reality is, there will always be those men who want to control our bodies, who want to control our sex lives, and who want to control our ambitions. Women and girls are still the victims of sex trafficking and enslavement in numbers that just\u2026 that are just a nightmare when you think about it..</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>And what are we, but living nightmares right? You\u2019ve got the power now, the real power to make a difference. Even if it\u2019s something as small as scaring the fuck out of a local politician to make him change his stance on reproductive legislation, or as visceral as ripping the lungs out of a gangster selling girls. </i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>You have that power, and more than that, you have a sisterhood that can back you up and, provide resources and point you in the right direction. Your family might have pull on you and obligations, but the sisterhood transcends that. We\u2019re all in this together, looking out for any nonmale in a fucked-up situation we know we can do something about. We help shelters get funding and past red tape, we make sure there are hospitals that are willing to do what\u2019s right for the women brought to them in places that want to dictate women\u2019s health. And we bring unholy violence and judgment to the forces that would imprison and abuse our less accursed sisters.\u201d</i><br /> -Donna Brick Breaker, Local Sisterhood Chapter head</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">As Donna says, the Sisterhood has existed in multiple forms across history and cultures under different names. The one uniting factor has always been Accursed women realizing they can use their power to better the lot of other women. The Sisterhood is active mainly in Western nations, but has \u2018sister\u2019 groups across the world.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Western \u201cSisterhood\u201d was last known as \u201cVictoria\u2019s Sisters\u201d during the reign of Queen Victoria, operating across the British Empire, before eventually becoming \u201cThe Sisterhood\u201d as the organization dropped its imperial roots to welcome women of indigenous cultures the British empire had conquered and incorporating with other similar groups that had arisen in places like North America.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Sisterhood then, is simply a multi-national organization of Accursed that seek to protect, promote, and assist the cause of women in all the places they operate. From volunteering, protesting, and providing funds. To using rituals, spells, and violence for the cause.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Organization</b><br /> <i>\u201cHmm, well of course at the top we have the main chapter in London. Agatha\u2019s finishing school for girls that dates back to the original founding of Victoria\u2019s sisters. Agatha is still in charge over there and the head of the entire sisterhood if we\u2019re being specific. But Agatha rarely takes a direct hand these days. She seems to more enjoy teaching the girls at the school and leaving the day to day business to the different regional heads.</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>The regional heads are known as Eldest sisters and oversee a main chapter house in an area. There\u2019s one in New York that oversees most of the North East coast. While the main chapter house in Montana covers the surrounding states, while California has two separate head chapter houses, one in the North and one in the South.</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>And then of course there\u2019s just the regular chapter houses. All ran by an elder sister, yeah, I know, not an eldest, an elder, it gets confusing, and their chosen council if they have one.</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>What do the chapter houses do? Several different things. They serve as safe havens for the women in our charge and care, as well as places of learning, staging grounds for missions, and homes for sisterhood agents. </i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Chapterhouses take many different forms, from women\u2019s shelters, to farms, college dormitories, and apartment complexes, to even a few liminal spaces that are safe and reliable we\u2019ve claimed. Some allow only non-men in, some allow women and their entire families to live there. Yes, we\u2019re a women first organization but that doesn\u2019t mean we all hate men, but that\u2019s a topic for someone else to get into with you.</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>At the most basic level we have Sisters, those of us who make up the majority of the sisterhood. Sometimes we can be the only \u2018sister\u2019 in an entire area, just watching out and helping our cause where we can. Sometimes you\u2019ll have entire crews that oversee an area. Whatever the case, all sisters are welcome in every chapterhouse the sisterhood has established. And as a sister, you\u2019re expected to help out where you can.\u201d</i><br /> Edwina Alberts, Sorcerer and Librarian at the Salem Chapterhouse.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>How do you Join?</b><br /> <i>\u201cThe sisterhood approaches you most of the time. The simple matter is, we\u2019re not everywhere, but sisters keep their eyes open for potential recruits, wherever the cause takes them. Most likely you were someone who was already involved in advancing the cause of women before you reached your Accursed status and continued that after your change. Or maybe we just saw the potential within you and that your heart was directed towards the right cause. In either case we bring you to the nearest chapterhouse where the Elder sister can evaluate you and see if you\u2019re seen as a good fit you\u2019re awarded probationary sister status.</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>During this time you\u2019ll be expected to perform what amounts to \u2018missions\u2019 and tasks to prove you\u2019re dedicated to the cause. These can range simply from volunteering your time and abilities to a local charity, to helping bring down a pimp whose abusing their workers. At the end of the probationary period the chapterhouse which sponsored you votes, and you\u2019ll be awarded full status or not.</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>After you\u2019ve become a full sister, you\u2019re free to approach our collective goals however you wish. New sisters can remain at the chapterhouse that sponsored them, travel to one in an area they think they might be able to help out more in, or simply strike out into new territory and work alone. Regardless you\u2019ll be welcome and recognized by all other members of the sisterhood.\u201d</i><br /> Edina Alberts, Sorcerer and Librarian of the Salem Chapterhouse</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Who are we?</b><br /> Among the members of the Sisterhood the primary make up are The Dead, Primals, and the Hungry. The passion among most Primals sees them championing the causes of those who may not be able to fight for themselves, The Dead may have been victims of injustice, and many Hungry can remember times where the laws were less favorable towards women. Outcasts with their focus on trying to return to different worlds often seem less concerned with trying to better this one, while modern Sorcerers are often too caught up in their own addictions and sacrifices to worry about doing so for a greater cause. This doesn\u2019t mean that there are no Outcast or Sorcerer sisters, just they are less common than the other three lineages.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Internal Politics</b><br /> <i>\u201cOkay, let\u2019s eat the Elephant in the room right now and get it out of the way. It\u2019s a brave new world we live in, and the definition of \u2018women\u2019 isn\u2019t the same for everyone. What does this mean for us? Well it means to put it bluntly, we have some members of the sisterhood who don\u2019t welcome our trans and nonbinary members and some who do. Just like we have some sisters who think we need a total exodus and separation from men, and some who have husbands, boyfriends, sons, fathers and brothers and still want them in their life.</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>We\u2019re not a monolith in our ways and thinking. It doesn\u2019t help that Agatha hasn\u2019t made any grand proclamations over it and let\u2019s individual chapters decide how they want to approach these things themselves.<br /> Honestly, I think Agatha knows any proclamation from on high would split the sisterhood up and weaken us overall. I happen to agree with her.</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>The one rule that remains the same, is anyone baring the mark of the sisterhood is duty bound to assist those who also bare the mark. Which means the most spiteful TERF has to help a Trans Sister if they are in the area and need it. Of course, that help will probably be the bare minimum, and all of us should keep in mind what the leanings of the local chapter are.</i></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>Most of us in the sisterhood tend to be I guess you\u2019d call moderates. We accept those who were AMAB with grace, and aren\u2019t looking to subjugate all men under a booted heal. But we do have some internal groups that have formed and push their own agendas.</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b><i>The Daughters of Lilith</i></b><i> are probably the most extreme group within the sisterhood. The Liliam at the sanest end just want a total separation from men, while on the extreme end wouldn\u2019t mind finding a way to eliminate all men. The name gives it away of course, Lilith the first woman, cast out of eden because she wouldn\u2019t bow to adam. Don\u2019t think they\u2019re genocidal maniacs of course, if they were Agatha would have them kicked out. They just don\u2019t see any use for men, and think the best way to handle the bad ones is through violence\u2026 and of course their standards for \u2018bad ones\u2019 are probably the broadest.</i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>On the extreme opposite side are those who follow <b>the path of Isis</b>. It\u2019d be reductive to say they\u2019re the most \u2018man friendly\u2019 of the Sisterhood, but there it is. Isis was the Queen of the Egyptian Gods, but more than that, she brought her husband Osirus back to life, and gave birth to Horus, both who did great and good things for men and women as a whole. The Isis girls see their role as healers and companions, but don\u2019t think of them as weak. They\u2019ll tear apart an abuser just as fast as a Lilian will.\u201c</i><br /> -Donna Brick Breaker</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Rituals</b><br /> <br /> The Sisterhood has a number of rituals that are available to members that help and champion their cause.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Mark of the Sisterhood</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Entanglement: 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Cost: Hold 2 Curse dice.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Range/Scope: Targets 1 individual who cannot self identify as a man.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Requirements: Very little is needed for this ritual, a pink marker or crayon to draw the symbol on the target. Some do take it further and get it tattooed. Roll with Artistry.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Effect: The target receives the mystical symbol of the sisterhood on a chosen part of their body. It\u2019s usually around 6 to 8 inches in size. Many choose the top of their hand, though on the shoulder is also common. The symbol is invisible unless the bearer chooses it not to be. All who bear the mark of the sisterhood recognize one another when in the close range band.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">One of us</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Entanglement: 4</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Cost: Bleed 3 curse dice</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Range/Scope: 1 individual</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Requirements: A ritual circle made with menstrual blood, a basket of eggs, a glass of milk. Roll with Medicine.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Effect: This ritual transforms the target into a biological Female version of themselves. For this reason, it doesn\u2019t do anything to those who are biological women already. In the past the sisterhood used this ritual as an ironic punishment for certain men, while in the present it\u2019s seen use among Sisterhood members AMAB. Not every trans or nonbinary sister has this ritual used on them, but it is an ability that\u2019s seen more use in the modern day, even on non-sisterhood members, than it ever did in the past.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Midwife\u2019s blessing</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Entanglement: 1</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Range/Scope: 1, 8 months Pregnant individual</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Requirements: Lemon Verbena Tea, Apricot Nectar, Almond Butter. Roll with Medicine or Survival.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Effect: Midwife\u2019s blessing insures a safe and easy labor for the person who ingests it. There will be no complications and the baby will be born healthy even at 8 months.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Woman Only Space</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Entanglement: 2</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Range/Scope: An entire building the size of an apartment complex. Roll with Leadership or Larceny</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Requirements: Sage must be burned in the area to be consecrated followed by a symbol of man burned in a fire.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Effect: Anyone who self identifies as a man finds themselves unable to enter the area, unless specifically invited in by the ritualist. The ritualist can designate up to their entanglement in others who have the ability to invite. The invitation can be revoked at any time, in which case the man suffers a major complication to all actions until they flee the area of effect. This ritual lasts for one week.</span><br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3769-orphan81","name":"Orphan81","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3769_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T15:25:16-08:00","id":1545968,"title":"","content":"I hope that Curseborne does eventually implement the multi-tier system introduced in Chronicles of Darkness, with the Curseborne core book essentially being &quot;this is tier one play&quot; and with supplements enabling tiers two and three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}